Probe DLL APBQuestProbe.dll SHA-256 580C457384A54B23811761F44FF0C8BBE0C17F7188AE5133AA126067B10D0407 (06:45 build; release DLL 01d4e1ed, trace DLL aba1d4f6)
Commands, one after the other (fifteen launches of two trials, split in three so that no single command ran longer than about an hour):
  build/catchup/run-quest-series.ps1 -Prefix qm-1 -Order off,acc,skip,skip,off -Trials 2
  build/catchup/run-quest-series.ps1 -Prefix qm-2 -Order acc,acc,skip,off,off -Trials 2
  build/catchup/run-quest-series.ps1 -Prefix qm-3 -Order skip,acc,acc,off,skip -Trials 2
Profile APB-CatchUp-Test, FramerateLimit 30, start save APB_MQ203_A, game window in front 100% in all 30 trials, dropped rows 0.
"off" = VM catch-up not installed (same mod list); "acc" = accelerate with the release read rule; "skip" = the same plus the test
rule SetSkipBlocked (APB_CATCHUP_SKIP=1). Ten trials per condition. Mean position of a condition in the order of launches:
off 7.8, acc 8.0, skip 8.2. The plan of 2026-11-10 had two conditions; the user chose three on 2026-11-11.

RESULT
- 30 of 30 trials ended normally. No loading hang, no stall, no failed load, no dump written.
- Identical in every trial of every condition: MQ203 stage order 20 30 40 48 50 60; stage 48 set after the graph event; all 30
  scene phases in order; 24 Esbern/Delphine lines in the same order (digest fdb15642cc); end state digest 995561791e; end state
  equal after saving and reloading; no end-state line differing from the first off trial.
- guard_violations 0 in all 20 catch-up trials.
- Catch-up at work: acc 2,165-2,584 extra cycles and 4,513-5,242 extra calls per trial; skip 4,377-4,760 cycles, 9,894-11,080
  extra calls, 14,930-16,567 front skips, the queue rebuilt after 5-10 cycles per trial (74 in all).
- Timing of the quest is the same in the three conditions (seconds, median with range):
    stage 30 -> 60:  off 180.3 (173.2-237.7)   acc 180.6 (171.4-206.3)   skip 184.3 (172.8-193.4)
    stage 48 -> 60:  off 78.3 (77.4-79.8)      acc 77.7 (77.2-78.8)      skip 77.8 (77.1-78.1)
    graph event -> stage 48 notification: 65-69 ms in all 30 trials (two frames at 30 FPS).
  The scene is paced by voice lines and packages, so no speed-up was expected here; the spread sits in stage 30 -> 40 and
  40 -> 48 (the scene phases that also varied in earlier stock trials). The three slowest trials are two off and one acc.
- gate_closes 0 in every trial (the counter cannot see loads: no VM update reaches the hook during a loading screen).

VALIDITY NOTES
- qm-1-01-off trial 1 (catch-up not installed): a MessageBoxMenu with the Cursor Menu opened at 84.2 s and closed at 87.5 s,
  between stages 40 and 48, and the player had moved 30 units. What opened and closed it is not known (nothing in the Papyrus
  log names it). The test plan allows only HUD and loading menus, so this trial is marked; its outcome is the same as the others.
  Without it the off condition has nine unmarked trials.
- One skip trial shows the player 10 units from where they were placed, with no menu and no package.
- Every launch left two crash logs 0-5 s after "quest probe complete", while the window was being closed: execute access
  violation at two adjacent 64 KB-aligned addresses (0x7FF5DF460000/450000 in eleven launches, another pair in four: three acc and one off, see the list below). The off launches have them too. No address of this project in the call-stack or stack section of
  any of the 30 logs.

WHAT THIS RUN SHOWS AND WHAT IT DOES NOT
- Shows: in this segment, with this mod list, neither rule changed the order of stages, the path to stage 48, the dialogue order
  or the end state in ten trials each, including the skip rule, which lets calls run ahead of earlier queued calls of other scripts.
- Does not show: an effect on quest timing (none expected, none seen); behaviour in other quests or scenes; 42 FPS; a save made
  while the scene runs (the mid-save runs of the plan are next); the release DLL (the probe compiles the same VMCatchUp.cpp and
  menu gate, not Plugin.cpp).
- The loading hang of 2026-11-10 (qs-a-02-skip) did not recur. Segment A totals, all builds: 60 trials; catch-up on 34
  (acc 18, skip 16) with 1 hang, off 26 with 0. One event in 34 against none in 26 does not separate the conditions, and in
  that process no extra cycle had run before the hang. Its cause stays open.

